# Code owners — mirrors the assignment table in docs/ROLES.md and
# docs/TEAM-EXECUTION-PLAN.md §3 (2026-08-10).
#
# GitHub requests review from the matching owner automatically when a PR
# touches these paths. Nothing here BLOCKS a merge: that only happens if
# "Require review from Code Owners" is turned on in branch protection, which
# is deliberately off so the team can keep pushing directly to main.
#
# Precedence: the LAST matching pattern wins, so the order below is
# general -> specific. Every owner must have write access or the rule is
# silently ignored.
#
# ONE PRIMARY OWNER PER PATH. Co-ownership was tried and removed: three names
# on a path means the review notification is everyone's job and therefore
# nobody's. Where a second name appears below it is a deliberate cross-check
# (security, an interface the architect must approve, or the R2/R3 infra pair
# added 2026-08-12), not shared custody. In every such case the FIRST name is
# the primary owner and the second is the cross-check.

